- when the user says `Read-only diagnosis` and asks for exact producer/test read-write evidence, stay in analysis mode and trace the actual code paths instead of proposing speculative fixes [Task 1]
- when the user says `Do not ask clarifying questions` and wants the full deliverable in one pass, finish the investigation and note environment blockers explicitly instead of pausing midstream [Task 1]
- when the user asks for an inventory of `each call site found` and says `nothing to do` is a valid outcome, treat a no-op migration as a correct end state if grep/typecheck/tests support it [Task 2]
- when the user says `NEVER run two concurrent full vitest runs`, keep Stratum verification serial and targeted [Task 2]

## Reusable knowledge

- `T2F5_SHELL_WRAPPER` already writes the terminal sentinel before exit; the observable inconsistency comes from `pollBackgroundRun()` scanning the stream and only then checking liveness if `exitCode` is still undefined [Task 1]
- `waitFor()` returns on the first matching status, so product-level inconsistent terminal responses surface directly in the test contract [Task 1]
- In this checkout there were no real `module.register(...)` hits under `ts/src`, and `ts/src/connectors/claude-bg-worker-hooks.mjs` already uses `registerHooks(...)` [Task 2]
- From `/Users/ruze/reg/my/forge/stratum/ts`, the correct connector-focused test scope is `tests/connectors`, not `ts/tests/connectors` [Task 2]


